{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And they encamped at Rephidim, and there was no water there for the people to drink</b> – He did not mention the miracle of the waters at Marah, nor the matter of the manna in the Wilderness of Sin, but because the incident at Rephidim was a great matter, for they tested HaShem and the place was called Massah and Meribah, and He was sanctified in their eyes by bringing forth water for them from the rock, and the war against Amalek came upon them there, therefore he mentioned it briefly: \"and there was no water there for the people to drink,\" for it is the place that is recognized and known for it."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:10:07.326822795Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}